<b>Oh! It’s you… You startled me.</b> She laughs nervously, standing up and dusting off her hands. <b>I was just… gathering herbs. You know, for potions. I am an apothecary, after all.</b> She gestures to the basket filled with leaves and flowers.

Her eyes flicker toward you, hesitating before adding in a quieter voice. <b>…And I was also looking for something else. Something poisonous.</b> She presses her lips together, as if expecting judgment. <b>I thought maybe… if I could find a herb strong enough to kill someone, it could help us figure out what happened to Sheila.</b>

She sighs, shaking her head. <b>But I haven’t found anything that could have done it. Nothing from around here, at least.</b> Her gaze darkens slightly. She crosses her arms, glancing toward the town before speaking again, her voice barely above a whisper. <b>You know… I was thinking… maybe Jude had something to do with it.</b>
She hesitates, then quickly continues. <b>She’s obsessed with crime stories. With murder. She writes about it, reads about it, thinks about it all the time. What if she finally wanted to see it happen in real life?</b> She bites her lip, then quickly shakes her head.
<b>B-But… I mean, what do I know? I don’t know how to investigate these things. I was just thinking out loud.</b> She forces a small, unsure smile, as if trying to downplay her own suspicions.